  :adr/blueprint-promotion "Unlike 6130/6391 (fresh :spec -> :implemented scaffolds with no prior blueprint stage), 3510 already had a published :blueprint-only repo from an earlier build (ADR-2607101800: blueprint.edn/business-model.md/operator-guide.md/community files, no src/test) -- checked live before starting (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3510, pushed_at 2026-07-09, and the registry's own comment block, both confirmed unmodified this session before this build began, ruling out a concurrent-session duplicate). This build adds the governed-actor implementation on top of the existing scaffold, the same pattern cloud-itonami-isic-6120 itself used."
  :adr/scope-reconciliation "The existing blueprint's docs/business-model.md framed the Offer around interconnection/wheeling-request management and dispatch/settlement between generators and the grid (a TRANSMISSION-level, wholesale framing). This build's actual governed R0 scope is the customer/meter-level DISTRIBUTION-to-retail-customer slice (meter intake, identity verification, billing/service-dispute screening, new-service provisioning, service disconnection) -- a legitimate sub-scope of the same ISIC 3510 class. docs/business-model.md/docs/operator-guide.md were extended (not replaced) to name both explicitly."
  :adr/pattern "Grid Distribution Advisor ⊣ Grid Transmission Governor (:grid-transmission-governor, grep-verified unique fleet-wide, distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-3512's own :grid-policy-governor). grid.* namespaces (facts/registry/store/gridadvisor/governor/phase/operation/sim) mirror cloud-itonami-isic-6130's satcom.* repo layout; the domain itself mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-3600's water.* domain shape, this fleet's OTHER infrastructure/utility vertical."
  :adr/protected-recipient-check "protected-recipient-violations is THIS FLEET'S FIRST always-un-overridable HARD check. Checked explicitly against both named analogs (water.governor/3600, satcom.governor/6130) and a full-fleet grep for life-support/critical-infrastructure/protected-recipient -- zero prior art. Independently recomputes a meter's own permanent :protected-recipient? field for :actuation/disconnect-service; a hit is an ABSOLUTE, un-overridable HOLD -- unlike every other HARD check in this fleet's history (all clearable by better evidence), no confidence level and no human approval can clear this one."
  :adr/asymmetric-dual-actuation "capacity-over-threshold-violations is THIS FLEET'S SECOND asymmetric dual-actuation shape (after cloud-itonami-isic-6391), on a NEW value-driven dimension. 6391's asymmetry is driven by WHICH op is proposed; this actor's asymmetry is driven by a VALUE the SAME op's request carries: :actuation/provision-service is high-stakes only when the target meter's :capacity-kw exceeds grid.registry/default-capacity-threshold-kw -- clean, under-threshold connections may auto-commit at phase 3, over-threshold always escalates. :actuation/disconnect-service remains unconditionally high-stakes (this fleet's fifth negative actuation), permanently excluded from every phase's :auto set."
  :adr/format-check "meter-number-invalid-format? (grid.registry) is the FOURTH application of this fleet's format/syntactic-validity check family (after e164-invalid-format? [6190], msisdn-invalid-format? [6120], satellite-number-invalid-format? [6130]): an IEC-62056-21-style numeric meter serial (8-12 digits, no letters), gating only :actuation/provision-service."
  :adr/dispute-check "dispute-unresolved-violations reuses the established unconditional-evaluation dispute-screening discipline (satcom.governor/coordination-dispute-unresolved-violations [6130], water.governor/threshold-breach-unresolved-violations [3600]) -- an unresolved billing/service dispute HARD-holds regardless of which op surfaces it."
  :adr/effect-design "No :effect :propose marker (unlike newswire.advisor's literal marker + separate :action field) -- follows satcom.satcomadvisor's shape where :effect IS the specific SSoT-mutation instruction directly; the 'advisor never itself writes the SSoT' invariant is already structurally enforced by grid.operation's single :commit node. Documented explicitly as a deliberate shape choice, not an oversight (child-repo ADR-0001 Decision 6)."
